<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds end lower on high US housing starts.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds end lower on high US housing starts.</headline>
<text>
<p>1550 GMT - Dutch bonds end lower on Tuesday, dragged further down after higher than expected U.S. November housing starts. Volume extremely thin as most market players are said to have closed their books. Hesitant attitude ahead of this afternoon's FOMC meeting.</p>
<p>* 6.25 July 1998 104.19/27, bid yld 3.44 pct vs 104.22, 3.43</p>
<p>* Sept 2001 116.53/63, bid yld 4.76 pct vs 116.68/78, 4.73</p>
<p>* Jan 2006 101.30/38, bid yield 5.81 pct vs 101.54/62, 5.77</p>
<p>* 10-yr yld spread vs April 2006 bund widens to -9 basis pts from -8.</p>
<p>* Jan 2023s 111.21/41, 6.57 pct yield vs 111.69/89, 6.54.</p>
</text>
